PS5 HDMI: 4K120 only where it can work, and back to 4K60 by itself when it doesn't

Borrowed from Slip's hdmi-usbc-test branch (Slip-Up/ps5-linux-patches, frl-detect.inc,
frl-native.inc, amdgpu_dm.c), on top of our Sony-sequence 4K120 path (Lawson):
 - 4K120 is offered only when the display's EDID announces FRL at 4 lanes x 8 Gbps or more
   (HF-VSDB or HF-SCDB Max_FRL_Rate >= 4) and YCbCr 4:2:2, and the HDMI chip's own report in
   byte 0 of its EDID notification (bits 3:1, the FRL rate it found) isn't 1-3
 - after a 4K120 setup the chip's 0x7019 bit 6 (set while it sends FRL; 0x43 on a trained
   link) is polled for up to 6.5 s; if it never comes on, 4K120 is withheld for that display
   (until another EDID) and amdgpu switches to the same size at the highest refresh still
   offered, then tells userspace to re-probe (gamescope keeps its mode otherwise: black screen)
 - the log says why 4K120 is or isn't offered, and whether the link came up
Before, a TV that announced 4K120 but couldn't take our FRL link left a black screen at
every boot until 4K120 was taken away by hand (hsgodd, kishy, pukason).
